• Stock is allocated to the same item in priority order.
Algorithm
1. Create area demand records and stock records.
2. Process urgency levels from 1 to 3.
3. Allocate the smaller of available stock and demand.
4. Update stock and calculate unmet demand.
Flowchart
Start fi Read stock and demands fi Process urgency order fi Allocate stock fi Update balance fi Report unmet
demand fi End
Pseudocode
START
SET stock and area demands
FOR urgency from 1 to 3
  FOR each demand with that urgency
    ALLOCATE minimum(stock, demand)
    REDUCE stock and demand by allocation
    RECORD unmet demand
DISPLAY allocation and remaining stock
STOP
Python Source Code
stock = [["water", 100], ["food", 60]]
demands = [
    ["North", "water", 50, 1],
    ["South", "water", 40, 2],
    ["East", "water", 30, 3],
    ["North", "food", 35, 1],
    ["South", "food", 40, 2]
]
allocations = []
for priority in [1, 2, 3]:
    for area, item, demand, urgency in demands:
        if urgency == priority:
            available = 0
            for stock_item, quantity in stock:
                if stock_item == item:
